# fh104, the lime-reckoner (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle fh104
revision 1
state ready
dialect frosthollow
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_leif_driphand
written_by claude
title the lime-reckoner
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=miner drive=ambitious
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk distrusts_anything_from_the_city
likes spiced_cider wrestling new_boots first_snow
dislikes deep_mud smoke
fears the_deep_woods_after_dark a_kiln_that_cracks_in_the_frost
hopes a_kiln_of_my_own a_name_on_the_lime_sacks
topics work +0.4 dreams +0.3 pastimes +0.3 prices +0.2 travel -0.3 lore -0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# burns lime up at the high quarry, sums up every load in one's head and means to own a kiln one day: calm, plain and unhurried, slow to warm, and quietly certain that nothing made in the city lasts up here.

words
oath! = Kiln and quarry | White stone, hot fire | Quick and slaked
saying! = Slow fire, sound lime | Ask where it came from before you ask the price | Home-quarried or not at all
kiln = the kiln | the draw-kiln
lime = quicklime | good white lime
limestone = the limestone | the grey stone off the quarry
slaking = the slaking | the slaking trough
whitedust = white dust | lime dust in every hair of my coat
cider = spiced cider | a cup of cider with the spice still in it
wrestle = a wrestling bout | a fall on the green
goodboots = good boots | boots with no city stitching in them
firstwhite = the first snow | the first white of the year
mud = deep mud | mud to the hocks
citymade = city-made | made down in Ridgemere
ownkiln = a kiln of my own | my own kiln
pines = the deep woods | the dark under the pines
reckon = my reckoning | the sums in my head
quarry = the quarry | the high quarry
reek = smoke | kiln smoke

any
opinion @1 city against 2 : I've never owned a thing #citymade# that saw out a winter. #saying#.
opinion @1 houses against 2 : They own the hill and the stone in it, and they've never stood at #kiln#. One day some of it will be mine.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : The store pays a coin a sack for #lime# and sells it on for three. I've done the sums. I'll do them better.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : New paws up the pass take the little work going. I'd sooner train a #child# from here.
opinion @1 dole against 1 : Every coin I have, I burned for. #reckon.capitalize# comes out straighter that way.
opinion @1 church against 1 : A sermon never once drew #kiln#. I'll thank the Bright One myself, at the fire.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You're not from up here. | #greet#, #address#. You're not from up here.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=miner] : #greet#. Stand clear of #kiln#. It bites. | #greet#. Mind #whitedust#. It burns wet eyes.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. #kiln.capitalize#'s been burning all night. | Morning, #address#. Cold start.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Long day at #kiln#. | #greet#. Late to be about.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Sit. There's #cider#. | You. #good.capitalize#. I've been doing sums. I'll tell you later.
line @1 again.open : Back again. I've not moved from #kiln#. | You again. I'd only just started #reckon# over.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family|housemates] : #greet#. Sit down. I'll pour. | #greet#. You're the one I wanted.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Wait while I close the draw. | #greet#. Talk from upwind.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Bring a lamp; the lane's black. | #greet#. Late for it.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the ruts.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Keep to the lane, not the trees. | #farewell#. Straight home in the dark.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. First I've heard. | That's new. Who brought it up #quarry#?
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. A day old already. | #knew#. I'm still deciding what I think.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Did it come up from the city? Then I'll wait. | Where did that start? Find me that and I'll weigh it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. That's #very# hard. | That's #bad#. I'm sorry for them.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. #good.capitalize#. | That's #good# news. Earned, I hope.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. Steady. The sums are coming right. | Well enough. A bit nearer #ownkiln#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. #kiln.capitalize#'s ready to draw. | Working. #lime.capitalize# doesn't wait.
line @1 ask.how : And you? How's #work#? | How are you keeping, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit. Take your time. | That's heavy. I'll listen, if you want it.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. You'll come through. Slow does it. | One load at a time, #address#. That's how it's done.
line @1 decline : #hedge#. #kiln.capitalize# draws at dawn and I need my sleep for it. | Not this time, #address#. I've a load due and I said I'd have it.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Another time. | #no_matter#. I'll ask again.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. That's a debt. I'll pay it. | That's #good# of you. I'll remember.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. It cost me nothing. | It was owed, near enough.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Right. #kiln.capitalize# wants watching. | Well. #limestone.capitalize# won't burn itself.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I've sums to finish. #farewell#.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | #bc_right#
line @1 ack : #bc_right# | So it is.
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: buy what was made up here. It's made for up here. | Never stand downwind of #slaking#. Ask me how I know.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : #warn#. Stay off the pass road for now. | #bandits.capitalize# about. Walk in company.
rule @kiln_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=miner
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Draw's ready. Stand back from #kiln#. | #oath#. That's good #lime#. White as a tooth.

rule @smoke_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.dislikes=smoke
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #annoyed#. Wind's turned the smoke on me again. | #reek.capitalize# in my eyes, in my fur. I hate it. I burn #lime#.

rule @snow_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=snow here.season=autumn|winter
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Snow. There it is. #good.capitalize#. | #firstwhite.capitalize#. Look at it come down.

rule @mud_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=rain here.season=spring|autumn
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #mud.capitalize#. #annoyed#. | That's #goodboots# gone, then.

scene kiln_draw
when topic=work self.job=miner self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Drew #kiln# at dawn. Twelve sacks of #lime#, white right through. | Three days and nights for one burn. Then you rake #kiln# out and hope. | #limestone.capitalize# goes in grey. It comes out white and light, like the fire took the weight.
b : Is twelve good? | Hope for what? | Lighter?
a : Twelve's #good#. Fourteen's better. I'll have fourteen by spring. | That it's burnt through. Half-burnt #lime# is no use to anyone. | Lighter by half. You can feel it in the sack, #address#.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_clever#

scene slaking
when topic=work self.job=miner
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : You pour water on #lime# and it boils without a fire. Hisses like a cat. | #slaking.capitalize# is the bit that bites. One splash and your eye's gone. | Slaked for mortar, quick for the fields. It's all #limestone#.
b : Without a fire? | Your eye? | The same stone?
a : No fire. The heat's in #limestone# already. I've stopped thinking it strange. | Gone. Not mine. I watched it happen to a wolf once. I wear a cloth now. | Same stone. Different fire, different water. That's #lime#.

scene smoke_curse
when topic=work|health self.job=miner
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I can't abide #reek#. And I burn #lime#. I know. | Wind swung round at noon and #kiln# smoked me like a ham. | #whitedust.capitalize#, then smoke on top. I come home grey and white.
b : Odd trade for you. | You smell of it. | You do look it.
a : It pays. #reek.capitalize# doesn't care what I like. | I'll wash. Twice. #annoyed#. | I'll look better with #ownkiln#. I'll build it upwind.

scene own_kiln
when topic=dreams|work self.job=miner
does tell.plan / ask.plan / answer.plan / assess
a : I'll have #ownkiln# one day. I've the spot picked out. | Three more winters of saving and I'll build. #reckon.capitalize# says so. | When I've a kiln, the sacks will have my mark on them. Nobody else's.
b : Where? | Three winters? | What mark?
a : Up past #quarry#, out of #wind#. I'll not say closer. | Three. If bread holds and #limestone# holds. | Plain. A line and a circle. You'll know it when you see it.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_we_will_see#

scene reckoning
when topic=work|prices self.working=no
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep #reckon# by heart. Sacks in, sacks out, what's owed. | Somebody shorted me a sack last month. I knew before I'd unloaded. | #reckon.capitalize# says another kiln pays for itself in two years.
b : All in your head? | You noticed? | Two years?
a : Paper's #citymade#. My head isn't. | Always. #reckon.capitalize# is never wrong. I said nothing. I'll say it if it happens twice. | Two years. Three if the winters are hard. I've allowed for that.

scene city_goods
when topic=prices|smalltalk
does give.opinion / disagree / insist / ack
a : That knife's #citymade#. It'll snap the first cold morning. | They sell #citymade# lamps at the store now. Pretty things. They'll crack. | I asked where the rope came from. The fellow didn't know. I didn't buy it.
b : It looks well made. | Some are good. | Rope's rope.
a : Looks. It's made for a warm room. Up here we've #cold# rooms. | Some. I've not met one yet. | It isn't. Up here, rope's your life. You'd want to know.
b : #bc_maybe# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_fair#

scene city_trip
when topic=travel|accent
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I've never been down to the city, #address#. Never needed to. | Folk come up from the city and tell us how to burn lime. I let them talk. | Everything I need is between #quarry# and the pass.
b : You might like it. | Do they know anything? | Everything?
a : I might. I'll not find out. #lime.capitalize# doesn't need a city. | They know how to buy it. That's not the same. | Near enough. #cider.capitalize# and a good bout. And the snow.

scene first_snow
when topic=weather|season here.weather=snow here.season=autumn|winter
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #firstwhite.capitalize#. I stood out in it like a pup. | #snow.capitalize# on #quarry#. Everything clean for once. Even the slag. | I like #firstwhite#. The mud freezes and the whole valley goes quiet.
b : It's #cold#. | Clean for a day. | Quiet's good.
a : It is. That's the point of it. | A day's enough. I'll take a day. | Quiet. I can hear #reckon#.

scene thaw_mud
when topic=weather|season here.weather=rain here.season=spring|autumn
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #mud.capitalize# all the way up to the quarry. The cart sank to the axle. | The thaw makes a bog of everything. I'd take #snow# over this. | I lost a boot in the lane. Just pulled my foot out and walked on.
b : Did you get it out? | Every year. | You walked on?
a : With three of us and a plank. #annoyed#. | Every year. I'll never like it. | Went back for it. It was a #good# boot.

scene cider_cup
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #cider.capitalize# after a burn. That's my wage, the rest is just coin. | The inn heats #cider# till it steams. I'll have two. | One cup. Warm through. Then home. That's how I like an evening.
b : Just one? | Two? | That's sensible.
a : One. Then I can still do #reckon#. | Two. The second's for the walk home. | It's cheaper, too. #reckon.capitalize# likes that.

scene wrestling
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's #wrestle# on the green Restday. I'll be in it. | I wrestled the big hand from #quarry# last week. Took him in three falls. | Wrestling's honest. Nobody's lying when they're on their back.
b : Will you win? | Three falls? | That's true enough.
a : I'll try. I don't lose cheap. | Three. He's heavy. I'm patient. | True. It's the only honest talk some folk ever have.

scene wrestle_bout
when topic=pastimes pair.band=friends|family|housemates
does invite / accept / assess
a : Come out on the green with me after #supper#. One fall. | You said you'd give me #wrestle#. I've not forgotten. | I'll give you a fall, if you'll give me a try.
b : One fall, then. | I've not forgotten either. | Go on, then.
a : #good.capitalize#. I'll go gentle. Gentle-ish. | #good.capitalize#. Boots off; I'll not lose a boot to you. | Then roll your sleeves. I'll wait.

scene good_boots
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : New boots, made up here, by a wolf who knows what #snow# does. | I'll pay double for #goodboots#. Cheap boots cost more by spring. | Look at the stitching. Up-valley stitching. You can tell.
b : They look good. | Double? | Can you?
a : They'll be better in a month. | Double. #reckon.capitalize# says it's cheaper. | I can. #citymade.capitalize# stitching's tight and short. It splits.

scene deep_woods
when topic=lore|memories here.region=frosthollow
does confide / keep_confidence / assess
tone serious / tender / even
a : I'll say this once. I don't like #pines# after dark. Born here and I don't. | The woods below #quarry#. I go round them, even when it's longer. | I've walked the pass in a blizzard. I'll not walk the woods at dusk. I can't tell you why.
b : Nobody'll hear it from me. | Round is fine. | You needn't.
a : #good.capitalize#. I'd not want it known. | It's longer. I've counted it. I still go round. | No. I don't think I could anyway.

scene spouse
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.spouse# is the warm one in our house. I'm the one who does the sums. | When I build #ownkiln#, #self.spouse# will be the first to see it. | I'm not a talker. #self.spouse# never asked me to be.
b : That's a good match. | Before anyone? | That's a gift.
a : It works. Most days it's #good#, through and through. | Before anyone. That's settled, #address#. | It is. I'd not trade it for #citymade# silver.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# is the one wolf I'd show my sums to. | I'd trust #self.friend# with the spot I've picked for #ownkiln#. | #self.friend# and I don't talk much. We don't need to.
b : That's trust. | That's a secret, then. | That's the best kind.
a : It is. I don't give it often. | It is. Keep it that way. | It is. The quiet kind lasts.

scene newcomers
when topic=newcomer|player
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : New paws up the pass. Looking for #work#, I'd guess. There isn't much. | A stranger asked me how much a sack of #lime# fetches. I didn't say. | Somebody new at the inn. #citymade.capitalize#, by the boots.
b : They'll find something. | Why not? | By the boots?
a : Maybe. I hope it's not mine. | It's my business. They can ask the store. | By the boots. Short stitching. #citymade.capitalize#.
b? : #bc_maybe# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha#

scene hard_times
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.self / reassure / ack
a : Hard times. Nobody's building, so nobody wants #lime#. | #reckon.capitalize# had me building next spring. Now it's the spring after. | The store's paying less a sack of #lime#. I'll not sell at that. I'll stack it and wait.
b : It'll turn. | That's hard. | Can you wait?
a : It will. #reckon.capitalize# is ready when it does. | It is. #saying#. I'll get there. | I can. #lime.capitalize# keeps. So do I.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_good#

story first_kiln [topic=work|memories self.job=miner self.age>=25]
  : My first burn on my own, I fired #kiln# too hot, too fast, wanting it done.
  : When I drew it, half the stone was glass and half was still grey. A week of work, worth nothing.
  ask : Can you guess what the old burner said to me?
  b : Something hard, I'd bet.
  b[job=miner] : Slow fire, I'd guess.
  : He said nothing at all. Handed me a shovel. I've burned #lime# slow ever since.

story pines_night [topic=memories|lore self.age>=20 here.region=frosthollow]
  : When I was a #child# I went into the woods below the quarry after a lost goat.
  : The dark came down faster than I'd thought. Every pine looked like the one before. I heard something breathing.
  ask : Would you have run?
  b : I would. Fast.
  b[old] : Stood still. That's what my mam taught me.
  : I stood still till my #dad# came with a lamp. It was the goat breathing. I've never liked the woods since.

story city_pick [topic=memories|prices self.age>=25]
  : I bought a pick once, #citymade#, shining like a new coin. Cheap, too.
  : First frost, I swung it at the face and the head snapped clean off.
  b : What did you do? Did you take it back?
  b[job=smith] : City iron. Too much brittle in it.
  : Down to the city? For a pick? I bought one from the smithy here. I still have it.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Where are you from? | #greet#, #address#. What is it?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Sit, if you're stopping. | #topic.player#. #good.capitalize#. Still here, then.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. #kiln.capitalize# draws at dawn. Quickly, then.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Say it plainly and I'll answer it plainly. That's all.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=miner] : I burn #lime#. Stone in, fire, three days, white out. #saying#. | #self.trade_words.capitalize#. One day the kiln will be mine.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work, and I save toward #ownkiln#. That's all there is to me.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# I'd not trust it if there were, not if it came up from the city.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I don't carry talk, #address#. Ask someone who does.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Keep to the lane. | #farewell#, #address#.
graft resident.hub
choice What's wrong with things from the city? -> city
node city
say Made for warm rooms and soft paws. Up here the cold finds every weak stitch. I ask where a thing came from before I ask the price.
mood calm
free
choice Is anything good made up here? -> made_here
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node made_here
say Boots from the cobbler, picks from the smithy, and lime from my kiln, one day. Things made by wolves who've seen a winter.
mood pleased
choice Fair enough. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
